r response rate than controls (58% vs. 20%)...\"\n        - P0146: \"In a phase I clinical trial (NCT03829111), CBM588 significantly extended PFS in metastatic RCC patients, with a response rate of 58% when combined with an ICI, compared to 20% with ICI alone^{27}.\" (Note: Contradiction/variation in phase mentioned: P0261 says Phase II, P0146 says Phase I. Also mentions retrospective studies for NSCLC).\n        - P0567 Table: \"Clostridium Butyricum (CBM588) Oral Renal cell carcinoma Ipilimumab/ Nivolumab Response rate was significantly higher among pts receiving Ipi/Nivo +CBM-588 vs Ipi/Nivo alone (59% vs 11%; p = 0.024) Human samples (N = 30) NCT03829111 Phase 1\"\n        - Conclusion for CBM588: Data exists for Phase I and mentions a Phase II trial in RCC (58% vs 20%), but overall materials consistently state these are early-phase (I/II) studies with small sample sizes. No clear Phase III data is presented.\n    - *MRx0518:*\n        - P0261: Mentions it's being investigated, no specific efficacy numbers given here.\n        - P0192: \"The phase I/II open-label clinical trial (NCT03637803) explored the synergistic effects... results have not yet been published.\" Later: \"A phase 1/2 trial combining MRx0518 with pembrolizumab met its primary efficacy endpoint in RCC patients, though the pharmaceutical company later withdrew from development due to financial constraints^{319}.\"\n        - P0494: \"Preclinical studies have shown that MRx0518... reduces tumour growth by 35%–51%... Currently undergoing Phase I/II clinical research... preliminary efficacy signals, including SD for ≥6 months in 4/16 evaluable renal cell carcinoma patients.\"\n        - P0567 Table: \"Gallinarum (Mrx0518) Capsule Solid tumor... Pembrolizumab Overally response rate of 25%. No dose limiting toxicities... Phase 1/2\"\n        - Conclusion for MRx0518: Only Phase I/II data available. Overall ORR ~25%, some SD ≥6mo. Development halted due to financial reasons, not necessarily efficacy failure, but no Phase III data.\n    - *Other strains (EDP1503, MET-4, SER-401):* Mostly Phase I or early Phase II. Small cohorts.\n    - *General Consensus in Texts:* Multiple sources explicitly state: \"Most clinical trial data reported are from early-phase (I/II) studies with small sample sizes; long-term efficacy and safety profiles are not yet established.\" (P0261, P0146). \"Early clinical trials have explored probiotics...\". \"Data are from small, early-phase trials; long-term durability and optimal donor selection criteria are not yet resolved.\" (P0261 planning summary).\n\n3.  **Address the Specific Question:**\n    - Question asks: Are there updated Phase II or higher efficacy data for specific strains like CBM588, MRx0518?\n    - Answer based on materials: Yes, Phase II data exist for CBM588 in RCC (response rate 58% vs 20% control), and Phase I/II data exist for MRx0518 (ORR ~25%, SD ≥6mo in some RCC patients). However, all cited evidence remains within early-phase (I/II) trials. No Phase III data are reported. The materials consistently emphasize that long-term efficacy, large-scale validation, and definitive answers on universal predictive signatures are still lacking. Development of some candidates (like MRx0518) has faced non-clinical hurdles (financial withdrawal), further delaying larger trials.\n    - Need to format quantitative comparisons carefully.\n    - CBM588: Group 1: CBM588 + ICI -> 58% (or 59%) response rate. Group 2: ICI alone -> 20% (or 11%). Setting: Advanced RCC, Phase I/II trial (NCT03829111 / Phase II mentioned in one source). Time: Not specified, just trial period.\n    - MRx0518: Group 1: MRx0518 + Pembrolizumab -> ORR 25%, SD ≥6mo in 4/16 evaluable RCC patients. Setting: Phase I/II trial (NCT03637803). Cancer types: Solid tumors (NSCLC, RCC, melanoma, bladder).\n    - I will list these precisely as requested.\n\n4.  **Structure Output according to Instructions:**\n    - `quantitative_comparisons`: List each group/result pair clea